icate","derived_from":[],"mentions":[],"attributes":[{"prop":"mgx:schemaDoc","key":"doc","value":"Module → Function/Class. A module's public-API (`__all__`) entry that re-exports a symbol defined or imported elsewhere — answers \"where is X importable from,\" not just \"where is X defined.\""},{"prop":"mgx:schemaToken","key":"token","value":"mgx:reExports"}]},{"id":"schema:predicate:mgx:asksAbout","label":"asksAbout","class":"SchemaPredicate","derived_from":[],"mentions":[],"attributes":[{"prop":"mgx:schemaDoc","key":"doc","value":"Session → any entity. A chat session's turn resolved this entity as its subject or cited it in the answer — which parts of the codebase a human actually asked about. A runtime observation (owned term, no SEON equivalent); references that no longer resolve after a re-index are dropped and counted, never guessed."},{"prop":"mgx:schemaToken","key":"token","value":"mgx:asksAbout"}]},{"id":"schema:predicate:mgx:hasProseTokens","label":"prose","class":"SchemaPredicate","derived_from":[],"mentions":[],"attributes":[{"prop":"mgx:schemaDoc","key":"doc","value":"Individual → word tokens (an attribute, not a between-individuals edge). The decomposed word sequence extracted from an identifier's name (camelCase/snake_case split) and any doc-comment prose, used by the prose-to-symbol cross-reference index to resolve free-text object terms that don't exact-match an identifier."},{"prop":"mgx:schemaToken","key":"token","value":"mgx:hasProseTokens"}]},{"id":"schema:predicate:seon:startsAt","label":"attribute","class":"SchemaPredicate","derived_from":[],"mentions":[],"attributes":[{"prop":"mgx:schemaDoc","key":"doc","value":"The `path:line` or `path:start-end` source location of a Function/Method/Class/Attribute/GlobalVariable — where in its Module the definition actually lives."},{"prop":"mgx:schemaToken","key":"token","value":"seon:startsAt"}]},{"id":"schema:predicate:mgx:dotted","label":"attribute","class":"SchemaPredicate","derived_from":[],"mentions":